    <ID>MayBeConst:Sax.kt$Sax$// When we pass the MAX_BUFFER_LENGTH position, start checking for buffer overruns. // When we check, schedule the next check for MAX_BUFFER_LENGTH - (max(buffer lengths)), // since that's the earliest that a buffer overrun could occur. This way, checks are // as rare as required, but as often as necessary to ensure never crossing this bound. // Furthermore, buffers are only tested at most once per write(), so passing a very // large string into write() might have undesirable effects, but this is manageable by // the caller, so it is assumed to be safe. Thus, a call to write() may, in the extreme // edge case, result in creating at most one complete copy of the string passed in. // Set to Infinity to have unlimited buffers. val MaxBufferLength = 64 * 1024</ID>
